1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,624
Your mother paid me to hate you. In our dystopian city, wealthy elites hire professional scapegoats to absorb their worst crimes.

2
00:00:09,924 --> 00:00:18,900
I spent my youth locked inside high-security isolation vaults, carrying heavy sentences for rich strangers I never even met.

3
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:29,040
My heavy brass collar logged every transferred felony while my real mother waited faithfully in our dim, crumbling apartment.

4
00:00:29,340 --> 00:00:36,468
Today, I finally paid off my final debt and walked home, clutching my clean slate certificate in my hands.

5
00:00:36,768 --> 00:00:44,976
My mother wept as she embraced me, whispering that I was her brave hero who saved our family from starving.

6
00:00:45,276 --> 00:00:51,852
While she brewed tea, I searched for an old photo and found a locked metal box inside her closet.

7
00:00:52,152 --> 00:01:00,360
Inside lay a stamped contract from the Scapegoat Registry, stamped twenty years ago, carrying my own baby footprints.

8
00:01:00,660 --> 00:01:08,940
She never birthed me. She bought an orphan to serve as a lifelong sacrificial shield for her actual biological son.

9
00:01:09,240 --> 00:01:16,704
Her real son is the city mayor—and my brand-new clean slate was just erased to absorb his murder charge.

10
00:01:17,004 --> 00:01:23,892
As police smash through the door, I wonder: if love is bought, who pays for your sins?
